# Privacy Policy for Turtle Atlas

**Effective Date: November 8, 2026**

Thank you for using Turtle Atlas.

This Privacy Policy explains what information Turtle Atlas handles and how. The second part lists the photographers and licences of the images in the app.

## 1. Information We Collect

Turtle Atlas does not require an account and does not collect personal information. It contains no advertising and no analytics, and it does not send any information about you or your device to us or to anyone else.

## 2. Information Stored on Your Device

The app keeps a few things on your device so it can remember them between uses: the name you may enter in Settings, your favourite species, the species you have viewed, and your best quiz score. They never leave your device. You can erase them with Settings > Reset progress, or by uninstalling the app.

## 3. Camera and Photos

The Identify feature can use a photo you take with your device's camera app or choose from your gallery. The photo is compared with the atlas images on your device and is never uploaded. Turtle Atlas does not ask for permission to use the camera itself: taking a photo opens your device's own camera app, which hands the one photo back.

## 4. Internet Access

Turtle Atlas works fully offline. The only time it opens anything online is when you tap the link to this policy, which opens in your web browser.

## 5. Children's Privacy

Turtle Atlas is suitable for all ages. It does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13.

## 6. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this policy from time to time. Changes take effect when the updated policy is published at this address.

## 7. Contact Us

If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact:

[axiomaragames@gmail.com](mailto:axiomaragames@gmail.com)

# Photo Credits

Turtle Atlas uses photographs shared by observers on [iNaturalist](https://www.inaturalist.org) and contributors to [Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org), under the licences named for each one: CC0 (public domain dedication), CC BY or CC BY-SA. Every photograph was cropped, resized and colour-adjusted for the app; no other changes were made. Photographs under a CC BY-SA licence are, as adapted, shared under that same licence. The photographers do not endorse Turtle Atlas.

Some main images, marked "AI illustration", were created for Turtle Atlas with an AI image generator because no suitable licensed photograph was available. The same applies to the title artwork, the logo, the world map and the anatomy drawings.


